{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.MonotoneWordTraceFactorizes","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic"],"declarations":12,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.tr_mul_branchMixture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.tr_mul_branchMixture","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L174-L181","doc":"On the trace itself: a branch-mixture letter `cp • g m + cm • ginv m` stabilises `H m` with\nconstant `cp z + cm z'`, so the normalised weight statement above is about exactly this letter\nclass. (Its normalised value is then `normalised_mixture` with `z' = T.zinv`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.bondCounting_of_uniform","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.bondCounting_of_uniform","kind":"theorem","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L159-L165","doc":"**Pure bond counting.** If every one of the `A − 1` bond letters has the same normalised\nweight `w`, the additive law `B = E₀ · Σ_bonds (−ln w_k)` is `(A − 1) · E₀ · (−ln w)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_bondEnergy","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_bondEnergy","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L149-L153","doc":"**The normalised bond energy is `ln [2]_q`**: `−ln(q/(q²+1)) = ln((q²+1)/q)` for real `q > 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_weight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_weight","kind":"theorem","line":137,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L137-L147","doc":"**The common normalised crossing weight at convention D is `q/(q²+1)`**, for both signs:\n`ν z = q⁻² · q³/(q²+1)` and `ν⁻¹ z' = q² · 1/(q³+q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_mu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_mu","kind":"theorem","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L132-L135","doc":"**`μ = [2]_q = (q²+1)/q` is the forced strand normalisation at convention D:** `μ ν z = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_nu","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_nu","kind":"theorem","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L124-L130","doc":"**`ν = q⁻²` is the forced writhe normalisation at convention D:** `ν² = z'/z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_zinv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.convD_zinv","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L115-L122","doc":"At convention D the negative Markov parameter is `z' = z − h = 1/(q³+q)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.branch_weights_sum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.branch_weights_sum","kind":"theorem","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L104-L107","doc":"The `(c, d)` form `c σ + d·1` of a production letter is the branch form\n`(c + d/h) σ − (d/h) σ⁻¹` (using `1 = (σ − σ⁻¹)/h`), so its branch weights sum to `c`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.normalised_mixture","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.normalised_mixture","kind":"theorem","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L95-L102","doc":"**Any branch mixture of the two crossings has normalised weight `(cp + cm)·ν z`.** The\nproduction letters are `cp σ + cm σ⁻¹` with `cp + cm = 1`, so every one of them — `σ`, `σ⁻¹`,\n`(σ+σ⁻¹)/2`, the colour-weighted average — has the *same* normalised weight `ν z`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.normalised_weights_equal","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.normalised_weights_equal","kind":"theorem","line":86,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L86-L93","doc":"**The normalised crossing weights are sign-independent.** With `ν² = z'/z`,\n`ν z = ν⁻¹ z'`: a positive crossing (weight `z`, writhe `+1`) and a negative crossing (weight\n`z'`, writhe `−1`) contribute the same factor once normalised. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.mu_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.mu_forced","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L80-L84","doc":"**`μ` is forced too:** `μ = 1/(ν z)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.nu_sq_forced","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MathlibExt.ForcedLinkNormalisation.nu_sq_forced","kind":"theorem","line":68,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/MathlibExt/ForcedLinkNormalisation.lean#L68-L78","doc":"**The two Markov moves force `ν² = z'/z`.** ","signatureChunk":0}]}